@@ -1 +1,27 @@
 # habits — a command-line habit and streak tracker
+
+Track habits with a weekly goal, mark the days you did them, and see your day
+streaks, weekly-goal streaks and a weekly report. Data lives in a JSON file.
+
+## Build
+
+    dart pub get --offline
+    dart compile exe bin/habits.dart -o build/habits
+
+## Test
+
+    for t in test/*_test.dart; do dart run "$t"; done
+
+## Usage
+
+    habits add read --goal 5          # register a habit (5 days a week)
+    habits done read                  # mark today
+    habits done read 2026-10-05       # mark an earlier day
+    habits undo read 2026-10-05
+    habits list                       # streaks of all habits
+    habits streak read
+    habits report                     # this week's report
+    habits --file ~/habits.json list  # use another data file
+
+`HABITS_TODAY=YYYY-MM-DD` overrides today's date. Exit codes: 0 success,
+1 unknown habit / already exists / not done, 2 usage error, 3 I/O or corrupt file.
